author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 600
acceptance_criteria: "The same recorded state, token budget and scoring version produce a byte-identical context assembly, proven by a determinism test and a deliberate-nondeterminism negative control; An assembly envelope names the point-in-time anchor, the scoring version, the token budget and the candidate-set filters that produced it; An assembly can be replayed later from its declared inputs and shown to match what the record supported at that anchor; A compact digest over the assembly and its declared inputs is independently verifiable against history without trusting the producer; Attestation is opt-in per call or per workspace and its cost is a by-product of an assembly that already ran, with the default read path measurably unchanged; Scoring changes bump a declared scoring version so an older attested assembly is never silently reinterpreted under newer scoring"
parent: pm-9rxu
